clear blue skies lost in a haze  and the once green forest of  southwestern turkey have been painted  black  the wildfire started on wednesday across  four locations in the province of  antalya  found by strong winds they quickly  spread to neighboring regions  but soon 26 provinces far  and wide began reporting similar fires  several people have been killed and  hundreds of others injured  thousands more have had to leave their  homes  the blaze spread through the highlands  and raged suddenly we had no chance to  flee  but when we were engulfed by flames we  had to run to the city of monavgart  then we came back to find the house like  this  more than 85 wildfires have broken out  since wednesday  74 of them are under control but the  coastal provinces of adana  osmania antalya mercin mulla and izmir  are still trying to put out flames we  are in manawgat which along with akseki  is ontalia's worst hit district  two firefighters have been killed during  operations here  while many people have been taken to  hospitals  at least 25 villages and districts are  evacuated  and another fire west in marmaris has  killed a 25 years old volunteer  who was trying to take drinking water to  the emergency crews  [Music]  the fires wiped out livestock in rural  areas as locals struggled to lead their  herds to safety  hundreds of homes have been destroyed or  heavily damaged  but the turkish foreign minister says  help is on the way  christmas  we'll start partial payments to our  citizens who have suffered damage to  their properties  we have begun transferring a total of  2.7 million dollars  from various institutions and ministries  for emergency needs  in antalya's manager district  although wildfires are common in  turkey's mediterranean  and asian regions during the dry summer  months authorities have yet to determine  the cause of these fires sabotage  we are considering the possibility of  sabotage and  any other sources of the fires starting  and we will carry out the investigation  to provide answers to this we will not  give up  until we have all the answers there are  concerns they may be a string of arson  attacks  targeting the heart of the turkish  tourism industry  the extent of the destruction will  become clear once the wildfires are  extinguished  but for those in the affected regions it  will likely take some  to recover and rebuild resources
 

